At review, pull request, and merge boundaries, read the learning gate policy. When disabled, do not create learning artifacts or block delivery. When enabled and applicable, require the project-owned brief, actual-diff explanation, five-question quiz, developer-authored answers, and current commit/hash verification. Agents may recommend enabling or disabling the gate but must not change `enabled` without an explicit user instruction.

Every schema 1.1 skill has an evaluator link. At task boundaries run only the deterministic checker. Route `input-invalid:*` to structural verification/recovery without effect evaluation or LLM. For `adapter-change|parity-fail`, require provider parity verification before effect evaluation and append a new `parity-fail` pending event on a pass-to-fail transition. Targeted evaluation may run only the deterministic reason mapping in `targeted.json`.

Before evaluation, freeze the checker JSON at `{{HARNESS_ROOT}}/evaluation/runs/<run-id>/trigger.json`. After every completed targeted/full evaluation, run the recorder with that decision file. A full ACK updates managed canonical/provider hashes and clears only the processed pending-event snapshot, preventing the same mandatory signal from reopening evaluation; newly arrived events remain pending. Load improvement after full evidence attributes a regression to the harness or an explicit evidence-backed user request; the request path must establish baseline/full evidence before applying a candidate. Gemini main orchestration owns the DAG; subagents return handoffs instead of invoking one another. Update the canonical contract before regenerating every selected provider adapter.
